        "# Module 4 — Supervised Learning: Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "**Predicting a number.** Same pipeline as Module 2, same discipline as Module 3 — a new kind of label, and a new way to judge the answer.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset:** California housing, 1990 census — 20,640 neighbourhoods (\"block groups\"), nine facts about each, and the median house price.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Three sessions, one table.** Every algorithm we meet adds one row to the same results table. By the end, the table *is* the lecture.\n",
        "\n",
        "| | |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| **I · Tue Nov 3** | Judging a number · the data · OLS · ridge and lasso |\n",
        "| **II · Thu Nov 5** | Tuning with cross-validation · one tree · random forest · the idea of boosting |\n",
        "| **III · Tue Nov 10** | Gradient boosting and XGBoost · what matters · the punchline on another dataset |"
      ],
      "id": "rkCO_xZ9x8sB"
    },
