      "source": [
        "### The helper: fit, judge, add a row\n",
        "\n",
        "Every model from here on goes through this one function. `log_target=True` wraps the model so it trains on log price and predicts back in dollars."
      ],
      "id": "ZW558dy8x8sH"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FASy2dvXx8sH"
      },
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "results = pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"target\", \"test MAE ($)\", \"test RMSE ($)\", \"test R²\", \"train R²\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "def report(name, model, log_target=True, prep=None):\n",
        "    pipe = make_pipeline(prep if prep is not None else preprocess, model)\n",
        "    if log_target:\n",
        "        pipe = TransformedTargetRegressor(regressor=pipe, func=np.log, inverse_func=np.exp)\n",
        "    pipe.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "    p_test, p_train = pipe.predict(X_test), pipe.predict(X_train)\n",
        "    results.loc[name] = [\"log price\" if log_target else \"price\",\n",
        "                         mean_absolute_error(y_test, p_test),\n",
        "                         np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, p_test)),\n",
        "                         r2_score(y_test, p_test), r2_score(y_train, p_train)]\n",
        "    return pipe\n",
        "\n",
        "def show(table=None):\n",
        "    out = (results if table is None else table).copy()\n",
        "    for c in out.columns:\n",
        "        if \"$\" in c: out[c] = out[c].map(\"{:,.0f}\".format)\n",
        "        elif \"R²\" in c: out[c] = out[c].map(\"{:.3f}\".format)\n",
        "    return out"
      ],
      "id": "FASy2dvXx8sH"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ff10L6Zsx8sE"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Evaluating Results\n",
        "\n",
        "Three numbers you will see everywhere. For a test set of $n$ houses with true prices $y_i$ and predictions $\\hat y_i$:\n",
        "\n",
        "| metric | formula | reads as |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| **MAE** — mean absolute error | $\\frac{1}{n}\\sum \\lvert y_i - \\hat y_i \\rvert$ | *the typical miss, in dollars.* Robust to a few huge misses |\n",
        "| **RMSE** — root mean squared error | $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}\\sum (y_i - \\hat y_i)^2}$ | *also in dollars,* but big misses are punished more. Always ≥ MAE |\n",
        "| **R²** | $1 - \\frac{\\sum (y_i-\\hat y_i)^2}{\\sum (y_i-\\bar y)^2}$ | *share of the variation explained.* Unit-free; 0 = predicting the mean, 1 = perfect |\n",
        "\n",
        "**We will lead with MAE in dollars.** A lender, a buyer, an airline — nobody acts on an R². They act on \"you'll be off by about $45,000.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "One more: regression has no threshold. There is no decision to tune after the fact — the prediction *is* the output. The judgment moves upstream, into the features and the model."
      ],
      "id": "ff10L6Zsx8sE"
    },
