        "### 10 · Random forest — many overfit trees, averaged\n",
        "\n",
        "Two ingredients, both from the deck (slides 71–86):\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Bootstrap.** Draw the training rows *with replacement* — a new, slightly different dataset each time. Grow a full-depth tree on each.\n",
        "2. **Random features.** At every split, let the tree choose from a random subset of the features, so the trees don't all ask the same first question.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each tree overfits its own sample. Their errors are different, so when you **average** a few hundred of them, the overfitting averages away and the signal stays. Bagging = bootstrap + aggregate."
