      "source": [
        "### 11 · Boosting — the idea\n",
        "\n",
        "A forest grows its trees *in parallel*, each ignorant of the others. Boosting grows them *in sequence*, each one correcting what the previous ones got wrong:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Start with a trivial prediction — the average price.\n",
        "2. Compute the **residuals** — what's left unexplained.\n",
        "3. Fit a *small* tree to the residuals.\n",
        "4. Add a *fraction* of that tree's prediction to the running total (the fraction is the **learning rate**).\n",
        "5. Repeat: new residuals, new small tree, small step. Stop when adding trees stops helping.\n",
        "\n",
        "*(deck slides 87–97: the worked example — Tuesday we walk through the numbers)*\n",
        "\n",
        "Small steps toward the right direction, hundreds of times. That is gradient boosting."
      ],
      "id": "Lcll6r4Dx8sJ"
    },
