        "### 14 · What matters? Opening the box\n",
        "\n",
        "A coefficient tells you what a linear model thinks. An ensemble has no coefficients. Two tools that work for *any* model:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Permutation importance:** shuffle one feature's column in the test set and see how much the error rises. If the model wasn't using the feature, nothing happens.\n",
        "- **Partial dependence:** hold everything else fixed, sweep one feature across its range, and plot the model's average prediction. The *shape* of the relationship the model learned."
